# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PWOS environment configuration
#
# Copy to `.env` and adjust. Categories below mirror the production rules:
#   Required            — must be set for production
#   Authentication      — needed when Google Login is enabled
#   Optional            — feature toggles / external keys
#   Development only    — local dev / tests (NEVER in production)
#   Disabled by default — one-time operator flags (leave unset in production)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Real PostgreSQL connection string. REQUIRED in production.
#
#   Local:   DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/pwos
#   Hosted (Neon — recommended):  DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@host:5432/db?sslmode=verify-full
#
# • Use sslmode=verify-full — it keeps the current secure behavior and
#   silences the pg v9 deprecation warning.
# • Serverless databases (Neon free tier, …) sleep when idle; use the
#   connection-pooled endpoint and the first request will retry while the
#   instance wakes up.
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/pwos

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Authentication
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Google Identity Services. The client id is public; use the SAME value for
# both variables so the browser button and the server token verifier agree.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-oauth-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-oauth-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# App mode:
#   personal     → never auto-load demo data (default; required for production)
#   development  → auto-seed demo data when the database is empty (local only)
# APP_MODE=personal

# Optional CoinGecko Pro API key (server only). Never expose this through a
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable; without it PWOS uses CoinGecko's public endpoint and
# reports rate-limit/unavailable freshness states gracefully.
#
# On serverless hosts (e.g. Vercel) the free public endpoint is often
# rate-limited, so prices can come back "unavailable". To mitigate this, the
# app persists the last successful CoinGecko quote (table `coingecko_price_cache`,
# added by migration `0005_coingecko_price_cache`) and shows it marked "Stale"
# during outages. Apply it with:  npm run db:migrate
# COINGECKO_API_KEY=your-coingecko-api-key

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Development only (never set these in production)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Embedded in-memory database — zero network, zero setup (great for local dev).
# Data is kept in memory and is lost when the dev server restarts.
#   DATABASE_URL=memory://
#
# In production the app FAILS CLOSED if DATABASE_URL is unset or `memory://`:
# it refuses to run on the embedded database. Use a real PostgreSQL URL above.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Disabled by default — one-time operator flags (leave unset in production)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Force demo seeding regardless of APP_MODE. NEVER enable in production —
# demo financial data must not enter a real database. The runtime hard-blocks
# automatic demo seeding in production even if this is set.
# ALLOW_DEMO_SEED=true

# Legacy single-tenant → multi-tenant claim migration (opt-in, disabled by
# default). When a legacy owner account without a username exists, public
# registration will NEVER claim it unless this flag is explicitly enabled.
# Enable it ONLY on the operator console while performing the one-time
# migration (`PWOS_ALLOW_LEGACY_CLAIM=true npm run db:legacy-claim`), then
# remove it. Without this flag, registering creates a fresh low-privilege
# "user" account and leaves legacy data untouched.
# PWOS_ALLOW_LEGACY_CLAIM=true

# System admin API token (optional). Grants owner-level API access via the
# x-pwos-auth header / Authorization: Bearer. Server-side only — never prefix
# with NEXT_PUBLIC_. Keep unset unless needed.
# PWOS_AUTH_TOKEN=a-long-random-secret
